#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:0
msgid ""
"Reference documentation for the plymouth-replace interface, which lets snaps "
"transition smoothly from the Ubuntu Core boot splash to a graphical "
"interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:8
msgid "plymouth-replace interface"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:10
msgid ""
"`plymouth-replace` allows a snap to provide a flicker-free transition from "
"the graphical boot splash screen on an Ubuntu Core device."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:13
msgid "**Auto-connect**: no<br/> **Super-privileged**: yes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:13
msgid "<br/>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:16
msgid "Requires snapd version _2.79+_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:18
msgid "Developer details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:20
msgid ""
"Ubuntu Core devices can [enable a graphical boot splash screen][core-splash] "
"implemented by the [plymouth daemon][plymouth]. The default behaviour is for "
"the system to return to text mode once the boot up process has completed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:25
msgid ""
"If the device provides a graphical interface, this can result in unwanted "
"flicker as the screen switches modes. The `plymouth-replace` interface "
"allows a snap to provide a smooth transition from the boot splash to their "
"own interface."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:30
msgid ""
"The expectation is that the snap provides a system daemon that will draw to "
"virtual terminal 1. If the daemon plugs the `plymouth-replace` interface, "
"it's startup will be sequenced to the end of the boot process where plymouth "
"would normally quit. It will also prevent plymouth from quitting at this "
"point, and stop a text mode login prompt from showing on VT1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:37
msgid "To complete the process some additional work is required from the snap:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:39
msgid ""
"The snap daemon should run `plymouth deactivate` before generating any "
"output. This will instruct the plymouth daemon to stop updating the screen."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:42
msgid ""
"When the snap daemon has first painted the screen, it should run `plymouth "
"quit --retain-splash` to instruct the plymouth daemon to quit without "
"switching back to text mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:46
msgid ""
"If the snap daemon fails to start, the system will recover by telling the "
"plymouth daemon to quit. This will return the system to text mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../reference/interfaces/plymouth-replace.md:49
msgid ""
"The [Ubuntu Frame snap][ubuntu-frame] uses the interface and can be used as "
"an example."
msgstr ""
